# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages rewrite rules. Unforced rules only fire when no
# static file matched, so /en/ and /fa/ always win on their own.
#
# There is deliberately no `/*  /fa/  200` catch-all. It looks harmless, but
# it answers every unknown URL with the Persian homepage at status 200 — so
# /fa/solutions/, /en/anything and every typo become indexable duplicates of
# the home page instead of honest 404s. Unmatched paths fall through to
# out/404.html, which both hosts serve with a real 404.

/index.html  /fa/  200
